# Citation metadata. GitHub reads this and renders a "Cite this repository" button, and it is one
# of the artefacts JOSS checks for at intake, so it exists now rather than at submission time.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Senbonzakura in your work, please cite it. If you cite a number produced by it,
  please also read the limitations page: several published figures have been withdrawn and the
  multi-direction idea this project began with is not supported by its own evidence; see
  the documentation's "what is and is not established".
title: "Senbonzakura: measured refusal abliteration for transformer language models"
abstract: >-
  Senbonzakura removes refusal behaviour from open-weight transformer language models by
  identifying directions in activation space that mediate refusal and orthogonalising them out of
  the weights. It ships the measurement alongside the edit: a harm-recognition score with held-out
  arms and seeded bootstrap intervals, null controls printed beside every result, a corpus builder
  that refuses to write a leaking split, and a contamination check against public benchmarks.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Iwugo
    given-names: Daniel
    email: daniel@themalwarefiles.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/elementmerc/senbonzakura"
url: "https://elementmerc.github.io/senbonzakura"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - abliteration
  - refusal direction
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - AI safety
  - model evaluation
  - large language models
references:
